  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "section": "narrative",
      "text": "Wellington X MF200 of 28 Operational Training Unit took off from Wymeswold for circuit training on 19 April 1944 and crashed at Normanton on Soar. All four men aboard died. The Nottinghamshire Roll of Honour gives the take-off as 02:30 and the crash about 35 minutes later; War Memorials Online gives 02:50 and a crash about 15 minutes after take-off. The sources do not settle which is right. The IBCC records describe it as night training and give no cause.",
      "cites": [
        "C1",
        "C2",
        "C3",
        "C4",
        "C5",
        "C6",
        "C7",
        "C8",
        "C17",
        "C15"
      ],
      "presents_conflict": true
    },
    {
      "section": "narrative",
      "text": "The pilot, Flying Officer Donald Hugh King, was 24. The Roll of Honour says he had about 1,500 flying hours but only 10 on Wellingtons. With him were Pilot Officer Douglas Robert Doyle, navigator; Sergeant Desmond Fretwell, 19, wireless operator and air gunner; and Sergeant Lawrence Emmerson Garrod, 22, air gunner. IBCC and War Memorials Online give Doyle's age as 24; the Wicklow heritage page says 25.",
      "cites": [
        "C18",
        "C19",
        "C21",
        "C26",
        "C28",
        "C38",
        "C37",
        "C47",
        "C46",
        "C29"
      ],
      "presents_conflict": true
    },
    {
      "section": "narrative",
      "text": "King is buried at Burton-on-the-Wolds, Doyle at Greystones (Redford) Cemetery in County Wicklow, Fretwell at Bradfield (St Nicholas) churchyard and Garrod at Blyth (Cowpen) Cemetery.",
      "cites": [
        "C24",
        "C32",
        "C41",
        "C50"
      ]
    },
    {
      "section": "community_connection",
      "text": "A plaque on a stone and brass pillar stands in a field beside the village hall off Main Street. It names the four men. A visitor comment on War Memorials Online says it needs cleaning of lichen and weeds. No source names who looks after it.",
      "cites": [
        "C11",
        "C12",
        "C13",
        "C16"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "photos": [],
  "custodian_status": "unknown",
  "notes": "IWM id 108496 in our record is dead. Search found no IWM entry for this plaque (hits were other memorials; 37427 is Rothersthorpe LN482). Not settled. ASN wikibase 153274 not readable (403 / certificate error), so not used. CWGC not checked, so no cwgc_url claims. Take-off time conflict 02:30 (Notts roll) vs 02:50 (WMO). Doyle age 24 (IBCC, WMO) vs 25 (Wicklow Heritage, which cites The Wicklow War Dead). IBCC lists the sortie as Day but also night training. Custodian: only WMO checked, which shows none; parish council not searched on a dedicated page, so left unknown not unknown-confirmed. Find a Grave and Traces of War not fetched."
}
